\section{What this data can and cannot do}{
The register links a person to a \strong{course}. It carries no group, team or
"Gruppe" column, so a participant cannot be placed in group A rather than
group B. Every group inside one course therefore shares the same
composition row. In the behaviour model
\code{y ~ card + (1 | block) + (1 | group)} these covariates are block-level:
they can compete with the \strong{session} random effect, and can never explain
the \strong{team} random effect, which has no composition variance to spend.
Treat any composition analysis as a between-course regression on as many
points as there are courses.
}

\section{Missingness}{
